---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Seery Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Seery TV series tracking app."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Seery Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: July 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Seery is a TV series tracking application designed to help users search 
          for TV shows, manage their personal libraries, discover new content, and 
          keep track of upcoming episodes.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains what information Seery processes, how it 
          interacts with our shared backend, and how you remain in control of your data 
          during our public beta phase on Apple TestFlight.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Sign in with Apple</h2>
        <p>
          Seery requires authentication using Apple's "Sign in with Apple" framework 
          to verify your account securely as an iOS and iPadOS user.
        </p>

        <p>
          This authentication process is handled directly through your Apple ID, and 
          your credentials are never exposed to our systems.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Storage & Backend</h2>
        <p>
          Seery routes requests through our secure, shared TypeScript backend application to 
          fetch TV show data. However, Seery is entirely database-free. 
        </p>

        <p>
          Your personal library, tracked shows, preferences, and tracking history 
          are not saved or stored in a persistent database on our servers. Your data 
          remains private and stays locally on your device.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Third-Party APIs</h2>
        <p>
          To provide accurate TV show information, Seery queries public data from 
          trusted third-party services, specifically TMDB (The Movie Database) and TVmaze.
        </p>

        <p>
          These API requests are handled by our backend as a proxy to fetch metadata, 
          artwork, and episode schedules. No personally identifiable information is 
          shared with these external services.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Library & Discover Features</h2>
        <p>
          Information related to the TV shows you add, search for, or view in the 
          Library, Homepage, and Discover tabs is processed strictly to deliver the 
          app's tracking experience.
        </p>

        <p>
          Because this information is stored locally on your device, your personal viewing 
          habits are not tracked, monitored, or profiled by us.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Upcoming Episodes & Reminders</h2>
        <p>
          The Upcoming page displays scheduled air dates for TV shows in your library. 
          When you tap the bell icon to set a reminder for a specific episode, this activity 
          is handled entirely on your device.
        </p>

        <p>
          Reminders are scheduled as local iOS/iPadOS notifications. We do not use remote 
          push notifications, and reminder times are never sent to our backend.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Analytics & Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          Seery does not sell your information and does not use third-party 
          advertising networks or behavioral tracking systems.
        </p>

        <p>
          Your search terms, tracked shows, and notification schedules are completely 
          isolated from advertisers and marketing profiles.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>TestFlight Beta Status</h2>
        <p>
          Seery is currently available as a public beta via Apple's TestFlight program in 
          App Store Connect. 
        </p>

        <p>
          Any crash logs, diagnostics, or feedback you choose to share through 
          TestFlight are governed by Apple's TestFlight Terms and are used exclusively 
          to fix bugs and improve performance before our official App Store release.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Since your tracking information is stored exclusively on your device and 
          no personal information is saved in our backend databases, you retain total control.
        </p>

        <p>
          Simply removing or deleting the Seery application from your iOS or iPadOS device 
          permanently erases all local application data, tracked series, and scheduled reminders.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This privacy policy may occasionally be updated to reflect new features, 
          platform updates, or adjustments to how our shared backend communicates with external APIs.
        </p>

        <p>
          Updated versions will be published on this page with a revised effective date.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy or how Seery handles 
          your information during our public beta, you can contact us:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--heading-small);
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 239, 231, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
